From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elkir0 <elkir0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/24] ARM: gts28ltexx_defconfig: Wi-Fi/Bluetooth as modules,
 LPASS, debugfs

- Radio drivers as modules, loaded after the initramfs watchdog guard
  (a built-in probe that hangs loops the board through RECOVERY):
  PCI_EXYNOS, CFG80211, BRCMFMAC, RFKILL, BT, BT_HCIUART (+BCM),
  BT_RFCOMM (+TTY), BT_BNEP (+filters), BT_HIDP, SERIAL_SAMSUNG,
  MFD_EXYNOS_LPASS (parent of UART3 and I2S0).
- Built in: REGULATOR_FIXED_VOLTAGE, PHY_EXYNOS_PCIE, SERIAL_DEV_BUS
  and its tty port controller.
- Bring-up aids: MODULE_UNLOAD, DEBUG_FS.
- gts28ltexx_m5.config emptied: its symbols live in the defconfig now,
  as modules.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_defconfig | 30 +++++++++++++
 arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_m5.config | 64 +++------------------------
 2 files changed, 37 insertions(+), 57 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_defconfig b/arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_defconfig
index d62f62dec..92d75aa67 100644
--- a/arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_defconfig
@@ -66,6 +66,7 @@ CONFIG_CMDLINE_EXTEND=y
 CONFIG_VFP=y
 CONFIG_NEON=y
 CONFIG_MODULES=y
+CONFIG_MODULE_UNLOAD=y
 CONFIG_NET=y
 CONFIG_PACKET=y
 CONFIG_UNIX=y
@@ -231,3 +232,32 @@ CONFIG_INPUT_UINPUT=y
 CONFIG_IIO=y
 CONFIG_IIO_ST_LSM6DSX=y
 CONFIG_YAMAHA_YAS530=y
+
+# Milestone 5, Wi-Fi and Bluetooth (BCM4358, docs/WIFI_BT_M5.md).  Every
+# driver that talks to the radios stays a MODULE, like panfrost: a
+# built-in probe that hangs (PCIe link training, firmware download) runs
+# before the initramfs watchdog guard and loops the board through
+# RECOVERY.  PCI_EXYNOS, CFG80211 and BRCMFMAC are already =m above.
+# The fixed-regulator driver and the PCIe PHY only map registers and
+# drive WLAN_EN at probe, so they are built in.
+CONFIG_REGULATOR_FIXED_VOLTAGE=y
+CONFIG_PHY_EXYNOS_PCIE=y
+CONFIG_RFKILL=m
+CONFIG_BT=m
+CONFIG_BT_HCIUART=m
+CONFIG_BT_HCIUART_BCM=y
+# Bluetooth profiles used by bluetoothd (serial, OBEX, PAN, HID).
+CONFIG_BT_RFCOMM=m
+CONFIG_BT_RFCOMM_TTY=y
+CONFIG_BT_BNEP=m
+CONFIG_BT_BNEP_MC_FILTER=y
+CONFIG_BT_BNEP_PROTO_FILTER=y
+CONFIG_BT_HIDP=m
+CONFIG_SERIAL_DEV_BUS=y
+CONFIG_SERIAL_DEV_CTRL_TTYPORT=y
+CONFIG_SERIAL_SAMSUNG=m
+# UART3 (Bluetooth) and I2S0 (audio) sit inside the LPASS block, whose
+# MFD driver creates their devices.
+CONFIG_MFD_EXYNOS_LPASS=m
+# debugfs: gpio, pinctrl, clk and regulator summaries for board bring-up.
+CONFIG_DEBUG_FS=y
diff --git a/arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_m5.config b/arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_m5.config
index b1c118738..c7b50da8a 100644
--- a/arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_m5.config
+++ b/arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_m5.config
@@ -2,60 +2,10 @@
 #
 # Samsung Galaxy Tab S2 8.0 LTE (SM-T715, Exynos5433) - milestone 5
 #
-# Fragment merged on top of gts28ltexx_defconfig by
-#   make gts28ltexx_defconfig gts28ltexx_m5.config
-# (run by scripts/kbuild-mainline.sh --fragment gts28ltexx_m5.config).
-#
-# The defconfig already carries the milestone-2 base (PMIC, eMMC, USB
-# gadget).  This fragment adds the Wi-Fi/Bluetooth milestone-5 symbols:
-#
-#  - Exynos5433 PCIe host + PHY for the BCM4358 (14e4:43ec), built-in:
-#    the Wi-Fi chip is behind it and modules are not usable at the
-#    milestone's rootfs stage (no module loading set up).
-#  - brcmfmac (BRCMFMAC + BRCMFMAC_PCIE) built-in.  BRCMFMAC=y also
-#    avoids a firmware/module request for brcmfmac-wcc (fwvid vendor
-#    ops for the 0x43ec/WCC match are registered in the same vmlinux
-#    when built-in).  Firmware loading at boot is not a problem: the
-#    kernel request goes through the usual firmware loader and is
-#    satisfied from the rootfs once mounted; until then the driver
-#    probes fine and only the firmware request waits/fails.
-#  - Bluetooth HCI UART (BT_HCIUART_BCM, which selects BT_BCM and
-#    BT_HCIUART_H4) built-in.
-#  - Serial device bus for the hci_bcm serial client (SERIAL_DEV_BUS=y
-#    because SERIAL_DEV_CTRL_TTYPORT depends on SERIAL_DEV_BUS != m).
-#  - RFKILL for radio kill-switch wiring.
-#
-# Symbols flipped from =m by this fragment: CFG80211 (defconfig =m).
-# Newly enabled (not set in gts28ltexx_defconfig): SERIAL_SAMSUNG
-# (no Kconfig default; needed for ttySAC3), RFKILL, BT.
-
-# PCIe host + PHY for the BCM4358 (mainline 6.12: PCI_EXYNOS is =m in
-# gts28ltexx_defconfig, PHY_EXYNOS_PCIE is a bool that depends on
-# PCI_EXYNOS).
-CONFIG_PCI=y
-CONFIG_PCI_MSI=y
-CONFIG_PCI_EXYNOS=y
-CONFIG_PHY_EXYNOS_PCIE=y
-
-# Wi-Fi: brcmfmac with PCIe bus support.
-CONFIG_CFG80211=y
-CONFIG_BRCMFMAC=y
-CONFIG_BRCMFMAC_PCIE=y
-
-# Bluetooth: hci_uart with the Broadcom protocol (selects BT_BCM and
-# BT_HCIUART_H4).
-CONFIG_BT=y
-CONFIG_BT_HCIUART=y
-CONFIG_BT_HCIUART_BCM=y
-
-# Serial device bus (hci_bcm attaches through serdev); TTYPORT needs
-# SERIAL_DEV_BUS != m, hence =y.
-CONFIG_SERIAL_DEV_BUS=y
-CONFIG_SERIAL_DEV_CTRL_TTYPORT=y
-
-# Samsung serial driver for ttySAC3 (not in defconfig, no Kconfig
-# default; Bluetooth lives on that UART).
-CONFIG_SERIAL_SAMSUNG=y
-
-# Radio kill switch.
-CONFIG_RFKILL=y
+# Superseded: the Wi-Fi/Bluetooth symbols now live in gts28ltexx_defconfig,
+# with every radio driver (PCI_EXYNOS, CFG80211, BRCMFMAC, BT, BT_HCIUART,
+# SERIAL_SAMSUNG, MFD_EXYNOS_LPASS) as a module.  Do not switch them back
+# to =y: a built-in probe that hangs runs before the initramfs watchdog
+# guard and loops the board through RECOVERY (docs/WIFI_BT_M5.md).
+# The milestone-5 device tree is exynos5433-gts28ltexx-m5.dtb from the
+# default build; this fragment is kept empty so old commands still work.
